1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:05,862
Welcome to advanced Playwright with AI. We will build regression evidence around one

2
00:00:05,875 --> 00:00:12,300
fictional transfer, using TypeScript, Python, or Java. Later, that same transfer will

3
00:00:12,312 --> 00:00:17,650
cross several local services and appear on a simulated terminal. Choose one language

4
00:00:17,662 --> 00:00:22,988
for your practical work, and use the others to compare architecture. Before opening an

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:27,388
editor, write the outcome you want to prove: one authorized transfer changes the

6
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:31,050
correct balance exactly once and leaves a traceable business record.

7
00:00:33,270 --> 00:00:38,070
Read the diagram from left to right. The browser calls the gateway on port three

8
00:00:38,082 --> 00:00:44,170
thousand. The gateway coordinates an accounts service and a ledger service. Accounts

9
00:00:44,182 --> 00:00:48,408
owns the immediate balance change; the ledger exposes a delayed read model in our

10
00:00:48,420 --> 00:00:53,832
distributed variation. A Python terminal adapter later connects to a local terminal

11
00:00:53,845 --> 00:01:00,158
simulator. These processes run on your workstation. They provide realistic automation

12
00:01:00,170 --> 00:01:04,020
boundaries, but they do not represent a production bank or a real mainframe

13
00:01:04,032 --> 00:01:04,845
installation.

14
00:01:07,064 --> 00:01:12,252
Open the laboratory contract before installing anything. The account and canonical

15
00:01:12,264 --> 00:01:17,426
transfer queries describe immediate business state. The distributed extension adds a

16
00:01:17,439 --> 00:01:21,776
separate ledger query with eventual consistency while preserving the business amounts.

17
00:01:22,639 --> 00:01:27,802
Keep those endpoints distinct in your notes. Otherwise, you may mistake an expected

18
00:01:27,814 --> 00:01:33,077
publication delay for a product defect. Write down which endpoint is authoritative,

19
00:01:33,239 --> 00:01:38,577
which one is delayed, and which environment your test uses. This decision determines

20
00:01:38,589 --> 00:01:41,126
whether an assertion should run immediately or poll.

21
00:01:43,354 --> 00:01:48,179
For TypeScript, work inside the supplied test project and inspect its package file and

22
00:01:48,191 --> 00:01:53,629
lockfile. Install exactly that dependency set with the clean installation command.

23
00:01:54,492 --> 00:01:59,616
Then install the browser expected by the pinned configuration. The laboratory may

24
00:01:59,629 --> 00:02:03,804
select an installed Edge channel for the measured run, while Chromium installation

25
00:02:03,816 --> 00:02:08,992
supports a separately configured Chromium project. These choices must match the runner

26
00:02:09,004 --> 00:02:15,204
configuration. Finally, record the tool version. Keep your approved package mirror

27
00:02:15,216 --> 00:02:18,541
configuration instead of changing registries during the lesson.

28
00:02:20,772 --> 00:02:24,860
For Python, create a virtual environment with the interpreter selected for the

29
00:02:24,872 --> 00:02:30,884
laboratory. Invoke its Python executable explicitly so package installation and test

30
00:02:30,897 --> 00:02:36,134
execution cannot accidentally use another Python installation. Install the pinned

31
00:02:36,147 --> 00:02:40,172
requirements file, then ask that same interpreter to install Chromium through

32
00:02:40,184 --> 00:02:45,672
Playwright. The pytest plugin will provide the page and context fixtures used later.

33
00:02:46,534 --> 00:02:50,060
Keep this environment separate from the terminal adapter environment when their

34
00:02:50,072 --> 00:02:54,760
dependency files differ; sharing an operating system does not require sharing every

35
00:02:54,772 --> 00:02:55,472
package.

36
00:02:57,686 --> 00:03:03,611
For Java, inspect the Maven project and confirm the JDK selected by your terminal. The

37
00:03:03,623 --> 00:03:09,474
project fixes Playwright, JUnit, and the build plugins it needs. Maven resolves those

38
00:03:09,486 --> 00:03:15,023
dependencies; the documented Playwright installation step provides the browser. These

39
00:03:15,036 --> 00:03:20,623
are separate from running JUnit tests. Keep classroom execution sequential initially,

40
00:03:20,836 --> 00:03:24,598
because a shared Playwright object is not an appropriate shortcut for parallel

41
00:03:24,611 --> 00:03:29,873
threads. If dependency resolution fails, solve the environment issue before

42
00:03:29,886 --> 00:03:33,361
interpreting any resulting message as a failed transfer regression.

43
00:03:35,584 --> 00:03:39,609
Start the local laboratory from the distributed project directory using its start

44
00:03:39,622 --> 00:03:44,734
script. Check the gateway health endpoint before opening the transfer page, and

45
00:03:44,746 --> 00:03:49,872
inspect the service output for startup errors. A page that renders a shell is not

46
00:03:49,884 --> 00:03:54,634
enough evidence that dependencies are ready. Confirm the documented environment

47
00:03:54,646 --> 00:04:00,334
metadata, then keep the services running for the exercise. Record the actual response

48
00:04:00,346 --> 00:04:05,434
you receive. The response shown in a slide is an expected example until your own

49
00:04:05,446 --> 00:04:07,496
request has completed successfully.

50
00:04:09,714 --> 00:04:15,564
Our API represents money as integer minor units. One thousand pesos is one hundred

51
00:04:15,576 --> 00:04:20,739
thousand centavos; the transfer amount of one hundred pesos is ten thousand centavos.

52
00:04:21,602 --> 00:04:27,064
The browser displays decimal currency, but server assertions use integers. Put these

53
00:04:27,076 --> 00:04:32,552
values beside each other before generating tests with AI. This prevents an attractive

54
00:04:32,564 --> 00:04:37,214
test from sending one hundred centavos while claiming to transfer one hundred pesos.

55
00:04:38,076 --> 00:04:42,489
Also assert the currency explicitly, because a numerically correct amount can still

56
00:04:42,501 --> 00:04:44,426
describe the wrong business operation.

57
00:04:46,652 --> 00:04:51,627
Create three rows in your evidence matrix. The successful transfer must leave a

58
00:04:51,640 --> 00:04:57,027
balance of nine hundred pesos and one record. The insufficient funds attempt requests

59
00:04:57,040 --> 00:05:02,902
eleven hundred pesos, keeps the opening balance unchanged, and creates no record. The

60
00:05:02,914 --> 00:05:07,677
idempotency case repeats the same request with the same key and must still produce one

61
00:05:07,690 --> 00:05:13,777
debit and one record. Give each row a fresh fixture. These are separate experiments,

62
00:05:13,990 --> 00:05:18,302
so a failed first case must never prevent another case from receiving its own opening

63
00:05:18,314 --> 00:05:18,827
state.

64
00:05:21,046 --> 00:05:25,408
Ask AI to inspect the contract and list missing information before writing code.

65
00:05:26,271 --> 00:05:31,308
Provide the language, runner, exact UI labels, endpoints, and expected business

66
00:05:31,321 --> 00:05:37,084
values. The model may help organize fixtures or explain a failing assertion, but it

67
00:05:37,096 --> 00:05:42,784
cannot establish that a test ran merely by generating plausible output. Keep generated

68
00:05:42,796 --> 00:05:48,434
code, reviewed code, and executed results as separate states. When a selector or

69
00:05:48,446 --> 00:05:52,946
response field is unsupported by your evidence, stop that assumption and inspect the

70
00:05:52,958 --> 00:05:55,684
actual application or documented contract.

71
00:05:57,912 --> 00:06:02,974
Now run a small browser check against the local page using your chosen runner. In the

72
00:06:02,987 --> 00:06:07,662
TypeScript excerpt, navigation opens the transfer route and the amount field assertion

73
00:06:07,674 --> 00:06:12,924
checks an actual accessible label. Authentication must already be supplied by the

74
00:06:12,937 --> 00:06:18,500
prepared fixture. This tiny check verifies the browser can reach the intended screen;

75
00:06:18,737 --> 00:06:24,000
it does not prove a transfer works. Save its outcome as a readiness checkpoint, then

76
00:06:24,012 --> 00:06:28,037
move on to business tests with clear starting data and the stronger assertions we have

77
00:06:28,049 --> 00:06:28,662
defined.

78
00:06:30,890 --> 00:06:36,690
Before continuing, explain the system aloud without naming a testing method. Identify

79
00:06:36,702 --> 00:06:41,078
who owns the balance, where the transfer record appears, and which process will later

80
00:06:41,090 --> 00:06:46,152
display terminal data. Confirm that your chosen language runs its own test runner,

81
00:06:46,352 --> 00:06:51,502
your browser is installed, and your local health check has an actual result. If any

82
00:06:51,515 --> 00:06:56,902
item is blocked, record the blocker instead of inventing a passing checkpoint. You are

83
00:06:56,915 --> 00:07:00,715
ready for the next episode when the environment and the business contract are both

84
00:07:00,728 --> 00:07:01,478
explicit.
